sentences.l:
But now, since then, Patroclus, later than you I go beneath the earth,
I shall not render you funeral rites before at least Hector’s here to bring
armour and head, of your great-hearted slayer;

But when then the water boiled in the gleaming bronze,
and then indeed they washed and anointed richly with oil,
and the wounds they filled in with ointment nine years old;

And her saw, coming forward, Charis of the sleek head-veil,
beautiful, whom the very-famous both-limbed one had married;
and she clasped her by the hand, and spoke a word, and called her by name:

then I would have suffered pains in my heart,
if Eurynome and Thetis had not received me in her bosom,
Eurynome, daughter of back-flowing Oceanus.

With them for nine years I forged many intricate works,
brooches and curved spirals, flower-cups and necklaces,
in a hollow cave;
